  <h2>AWD system overview</h2>
  <p>The AWD system distributes drive torque between the front and rear axles as operating conditions require. Diagnosis and service depend on the exact hardware and control strategy fitted to this car. Do not assume a particular coupling, gear ratio, fluid, or maintenance interval based solely on the AWD badge.</p>

  <h2>What to verify before ordering parts or fluid</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Engine code and production date.</li>
    <li>Transmission model/code and software version.</li>
    <li>Angle gear/bevel gear and rear drive unit identification.</li>
    <li>Propeller shaft and related hardware application.</li>
    <li>Brake package and rotor dimensions.</li>
    <li>Factory wheel and tire package.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Identification sources</h2>
  <p>Use the VIN with an authorized Volvo parts/service source or reliable VIN-specific build record. Keep the full VIN private; do not publish it on this website or in public GitHub issues.</p>
